  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PhysDisc 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You recently started collaborating with a research team at your cancer
    center to identify potential drug targets for a new study. During a patient education
    session, you discuss how physicians work with research teams early-on to provide
    helpful insights. One patient raises their hand to ask you, \u201CI thought that
    every person on a research team must also be a physician?\u201D\r\n\r\nIs this
    true or false?\r\n"
  explanation: "Research teams are typically multidisciplinary, including laboratory
    scientists, pharmacologists, chemists, biostatisticians, and molecular biologists.
    Each specialist brings skills essential for understanding disease mechanisms,
    designing compounds, and analyzing data. Physicians contribute a critical clinical
    perspective, but many aspects of early drug discovery\u2014like synthesizing
    compounds or running experiments\u2014fall outside their day-to-day expertise.
    Combining the knowledge of physicians with other experts ensures research is
    both scientifically rigorous and clinically relevant."
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
